  "_findings": [
    "The spectral-norm control loses to every other arm including no regularisation, 10 of 10, and costs 46 per cent of task-A capability. The advantage is not dominant-direction shrinkage.",
    "The published configuration replicates with a disjoint tuning seed: 0.2402 against 0.1750 for no regularisation, 8 wins to 1 with one tie.",
    "L2-SP, absent from the published baselines and equally free of previous-task data, is not separated from it: 6 wins to 3 with one tie, sign test p = 0.254, Wilcoxon p = 0.049.",
    "The two have opposite profiles: the regulariser raises task-A capability while L2-SP is neutral on it, and L2-SP reaches a higher retention ratio.",
    "The strength sweep on a single seed is unreliable: for the published arm it selected 0.1, which evaluates to 0.1994 against 0.2402 for the inherited 0.03, winning on 2 of 10 seeds. Both are reported."
  ],
  "_known_gaps": [
    "The l2sp cells do not record their multiplier in the per-cell output: the harness writes omega_target for the omega arms but has no equivalent field for L2SP_LAMBDA. The value reported here, 1.0, comes from the launch command and from the sweep file, not from the cells. Fixed for future runs.",
    "wd and ewc were not re-run in this session. Their figures in the published table come from a different session, without the perplexity and plasticity columns, and with tuning seeds inside the evaluation set.",
    "Run-to-run standard deviation on the retention ratio was measured at 0.104 in this harness, so mean differences below roughly 0.066 are not distinguishable at ten seeds."
